Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:47:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Merge guards for the port series, and the env-switch registry
 rows filled in

The regression net (patch port 0075, group R of the port inventory), adapted from the Tiaoge-tou/nxnative fork.

dm/tools/tests/test_merge_guards.py guards the port series' load-bearing pieces against a silent loss in an upstream sync: the Silksong fpslock row beside upstream's rows, the display-rate servo coexisting with the Frostbite tick (in this tree's guarded form), the settings table's skin and frame-rate rows, and the two games' profile keys. Adapted to this tree: the old fork's BC guards are dropped (BC here is the queue's own patch 0008, guarded by its own tests), the Dark Souls profile asserts are dropped (not this project's game), and the workflow guard waits for Phase 3's repository-level workflow.

docs/env_switches.tsv: the nine switches the port series reads (DM_PAD_SKIN, DM_PAD_BAG, DM_PAD_HADES, DM_SILK_SKIN, DM_HADES_SKIN, DM_RENDER_WIDTH, DM_RENDER_WIDTH_HD, DM_RENDER_HEIGHT, DM_SERVE_NARROW) had generated rows with no meaning; the meanings are filled in, so env_switches.py --check now flags only the two blanks that predate the series (DM_FONT_CACHE, DM_SHARED_FONT_SMALL).

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: Merge guards and env-switch registry for the port series (PROJECT.md Phase 2)
Issue: Tiaoge-tou/NX2Apple PROJECT.md Phase 2

---
 dm/tools/tests/test_merge_guards.py | 55 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 docs/env_switches.tsv               | 11 ++++++
 2 files changed, 66 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 dm/tools/tests/test_merge_guards.py

diff --git a/dm/tools/tests/test_merge_guards.py b/dm/tools/tests/test_merge_guards.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e055ba4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dm/tools/tests/test_merge_guards.py
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+"""Guards for this fork's own changes, which upstream does not carry: an upstream sync re-applies the patch
+queue, and a change can be lost without a conflict when upstream edits the same file -- the loss only shows
+on a device. Each test names one change of the port series (patches 0061-0076) and the file it must survive
+in: the display-rate serving beside upstream's Frostbite rate in the fps lock, the launcher's skin rows in
+the settings table, and the two games' profile keys. The old fork's BC guards are not here: BC in this tree
+is the queue's own patch 0008, guarded by its own tests, and the IPA workflow guard waits for the workflow
+itself (Phase 3, a repository file, not an engine patch)."""
+from pathlib import Path
+import unittest
+
+REPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]
+
+
+def read(rel):
+    return (REPO / rel).read_text(encoding='utf-8')
+
+
+class FpsLock(unittest.TestCase):
+    @classmethod
+    def setUpClass(cls):
+        cls.src = read('dm/host/hle_fpslock.c')
+
+    def test_both_sides_rows_survive(self):
+        self.assertIn('"fc9ea4ccc955d5799f37752b2d730b31", "Unity targetFrameRate"', self.src)   # the fork's: Silksong
+        self.assertIn('"799d1061182c1302e08e706b84ce76e5", "Criterion 60 fps mode"', self.src)   # upstream's: Need for Speed
+        self.assertIn('"a48c0de3bc353efa0e4d359bde05ef24", "FIFA frame regulator"', self.src)   # upstream's: EA SPORTS FC
+
+    def test_display_rate_serving_and_frostbite_tick_coexist(self):
+        self.assertIn('int dtgt = dm_display_hz() == 120 ? 120 : 0;', self.src)
+        self.assertIn('if (fb.n && target) fb_tick(target, src);', self.src)   # the fork's guard: no fixed target, no Frostbite write
+
+
+class SettingsTable(unittest.TestCase):
+    def test_skin_rows_and_enc_thread_default(self):
+        rows = {line.split('\t')[0]: line for line in read('dm/games/settings.tsv').splitlines() if line and not line.startswith('#')}
+        self.assertIn('DM_HADES_SKIN', rows)
+        self.assertIn('DM_SILK_SKIN', rows)
+        self.assertIn('SS_DISPLAY_HZ', rows)
+        self.assertIn('DM_GAME_ENC_THREAD', rows['DM_NVN_ENC_THREAD'])
+
+
+class GameProfiles(unittest.TestCase):
+    def test_profile_keys_survive(self):
+        hades = read('dm/games/0100A00019DE0000/game.tsv')
+        self.assertIn('display_wide', hades)
+        self.assertIn('serve_patch', hades)
+        self.assertIn('romfs_patch', hades)
+        silk = read('dm/games/010013C00E930000/game.tsv')
+        self.assertIn('pad_skin_toggle', silk)
+        self.assertIn('serve_patch', silk)
+        self.assertIn('display_hz', silk)
+
+
+if __name__ == '__main__':
+    unittest.main()
